Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||04-06-2000||08:24 AM||||Does anybody know of the prothane engine/tranny mounts that I can buy?  I'm looking for mounts that I don't have to press on (or is it an easy changeout from stock rubber to the prothane).<P>Haven't done this before, so I am interested in what anybody else has ran into.  I know fierostore has the kits, but it looks like I will have to do some pressing which is what I am trying to avoid.  <P>Who knows, I may not be able to avoid putting them together myself.  That's why I am here.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88 Fiero||04-06-2000||03:35 PM||||Boiler...contact Chris West of West Coast Fieros...he got a tranny mount that is mounted solid in the chassis preventing it from moving...much better than prothane...||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-07-2000||02:50 AM||||Be aware that the urethane bushings are designed to be HOLD that engine down. I drove a 4 cyl with solid urethane mounts. Very solid performance. If you like all the vibrations...||||reg||6
